summary.description:
**Thermostats heard:** {thermostats}

**Window contacts heard:** {contacts}

The number in brackets is the signal strength, which helps to tell your devices from those of a neighbor. You can ignore a device of a neighbor later in the options. A device that is missing is added automatically as soon as it sends, so you can set up now and wait for it.

The devices listed here become devices in Home Assistant when their next telegram arrives, so the naming dialog that follows does not list them. Name them later on their device page under **Settings** > **Devices & services** > **Devices**.

If window contacts were heard, each one gets a field below where you choose whether it watches a window or a door, because a contact cannot tell. A contact also belongs to a thermostat, but neither of them tells which. When the devices have sent for a while, you can assign each contact to its thermostat, and change the window or door choice, under **Settings** > **Devices & services** > **culfw (CUL)** > **Configure**.

The integration also adds the week program card to your dashboards, so that you can see and edit the week program of a thermostat. You can turn that off later under **Settings** > **Devices & services** > **culfw (CUL)** > **Configure**.

progress.listen:
Devices appear when they send. Thermostats send about every 2 minutes, window contacts about every 4 minutes. A thermostat with empty batteries or with `CEnt` not on `On` does not appear. You can add it later: the integration adds new devices automatically (option) or lists them as candidates.

This takes about {minutes} minutes. If you close this dialog, the setup is cancelled.

